\subsection{Terminal causal result: separated support discovery}

The completed MathIR ablation isolates the singleton actuator from its
proposal-capable execution plumbing. Both arms use the same \xdr{} objective;
only the treatment may place one entropy-gated alternative in separated replay
support.

\begin{table}[H]
  \centering
  \small
  \begin{tabular}{@{}lrrr@{}}
    \toprule
    \textbf{Terminal pass 12 metric} & \textbf{actuator off} &
    \textbf{separated support} & \textbf{paired mean $\Delta$} \\
    \midrule
    greedy \texttt{pass@1} & .7708 & .7969 & +.0260 \\
    \texttt{mean@8} & .7397 & .7699 & +.0301 \\
    \texttt{pass@8} & .8555 & .8822 & +.0267 \\
    \texttt{distinct@8} & .9102 & 1.0469 & +.1367 \\
    bank support per prompt & 1.3556 & 1.4821 & +.1265 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
  \caption{\textbf{Terminal MathIR causal ablation.} Each mean contains three
  paired seeds. Greedy, \texttt{pass@8}, and \texttt{distinct@8} improve in
  all three pairs; \texttt{mean@8} improves in two.}
  \label{tab:actuator}
\end{table}

All six runs reach the registered 12-pass endpoint and all 49 fixed evaluation
points. The treatment records 327 audited interventions. Proposal rows sent to
PPO are exactly zero, and proposal-only outcomes remain outside the on-policy
count table. The evidence therefore supports the narrow causal statement that
separated support discovery improves the \xdr{} system on MathIR. Other-domain
actuator cells are incomplete and are not claimed.

\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Executable identity is central.}
An outcome-entropy objective is only as meaningful as its equivalence relation:
strings reward formatting, while final answers erase alternative procedures.
\mb{} instead binds identity to the same execution that establishes correctness,
and \xdr{} optimizes that auditable object.

\paragraph{Discovery, balance, and entropy play different roles.}
Balancing cannot recover an absent mode, while rewarding every new string invites
error variety. The open-set bucket retains unknown support, one-time credit pays
for expansion, and replay preserves verified discoveries. Token entropy may aid
local exploration, but \xdr's empirical bank is specifically an online surrogate
for entropy over correct executed outcomes.

\paragraph{The evidence fixes the scope.}
The shared-checkpoint result motivates the method but is not a completed
campaign analysis, and the actuator result is causal only for MathIR. A
legitimate next test needs larger models, a fresh complete cohort, and new
independently executable multi-mode domains.

\section{Limitations and Broader Impact}
\label{sec:limitations}

The broad comparison is incomplete: domains stop at different shared passes,
no partial AUC is confirmatory, and three seeds establish paired directions
rather than population-level uncertainty. Because the method followed extensive
exploratory development, this effect remains hypothesis-generating despite
frozen checkpoints and audits.

All four domains are synthetic, the model has 0.5B parameters, and exact mode
identity is unusually available. Real proofs and programs can contain
meaningful equivalences no canonicalizer resolves. MathIR trades naturalness
for exact execution. Outside these environments, unsupported semantic strategy
labels remain beyond the scope of our claims.

Python factors admits only a bounded call-free AST, removes builtins, runs in a
separate worker on frozen inputs, enforces a timeout, and fails closed. It is
not a general code sandbox.

Diversity is not always desirable: valid modes can differ in cost, clarity,
robustness, or risk, and a uniform bank can overvalue poor alternatives.
Deployments should report correctness, invalidity, breadth, and the mode mapping
together, weighting modes by application value when appropriate.

\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Dr.GRPO can improve binary reward while the distribution of correct solutions
collapses. We define the failure on verifier-positive execution keys, make it
measurable with \mb, and introduce \xdr{} as an online open-set outcome-MaxEnt
intervention. The broad surface shows greater search success and breadth, and
the terminal MathIR ablation supports separated discovery. Diverse reasoning
requires both the metric and the optimizer to act on verified solution modes
rather than strings.

