\section{Algorithmic Details}
\label{app:algorithm}

Each optimizer update follows this order:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item sample one on-policy group and freeze the prompt's pre-group bank;
  \item execute every response, intersect validation with positive reward, and
  assign keys only to agreed validator-positive rows;
  \item compute the centered Dr.GRPO task advantage;
  \item compute rare-mode advantages under the detached open-set predictor;
  \item split one discovery credit across duplicates of each first-seen key;
  \item optionally generate one eligible separated-support proposal, revalidate
  it, and keep it outside PPO and on-policy counts;
  \item commit neutral discoveries to the count bank after group scoring;
  \item choose one accumulated bank by checkpointed global round robin;
  \item add verified-mass replay and, for multi-key banks, balance replay; and
  \item update the policy, controller EMAs, bank, and scheduler cursor, then
  checkpoint all states together.
\end{enumerate}

With one scheduled bank and replay capacity 16, the implementation scales the
replay contribution as
\[
  \frac{15}{16}\frac{1}{16}
  \left(\mu_t L_{\mathrm{mass}}+\alpha_t L_{\mathrm{balance}}\right).
\]
The historical prompt-local bank-entropy channel is disabled
(\texttt{bank\_alpha}$=0$); the open-set advantage is the sole outcome-entropy
channel in the actor advantage. Direct token entropy is absent from the final
objective.

