\path{paper/preregistration/e61r1_e58_vs_grpo_05b_12pass.md}. The clean
eight-row surface and its running four-row Stage-A block are bound by
\path{docs/clean_05b_maxent_vs_drgrpo_eight_environment_plan.md} and
\path{paper/preregistration/e70_clean_verified_maxent_vs_compute_matched_drgrpo_stage_a_05b.md}; the objective is
\path{paper/preregistration/e58_global_verified_replay_canonical_05b.md}; the
same-plumbing control and separated-support treatment are
\path{paper/preregistration/e66_same_plumbing_actuator_ablation_05b.md} and
\path{paper/preregistration/e68_separated_support_actuator_ablation_05b.md}.

The environments are implemented in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/canonical_actions.py},
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/python_modebench.py}, and
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/mathir.py}. The external Python process boundary is in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/python_modebench_process.py} and its worker in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/python_modebench_worker.py}. The open-set signal is in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/semantic_shannon.py}, replay in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/canonical_replay.py}, the bank in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/online_canonical_bank.py}, and the separated actuator in
\path{src/oat_drgrpo/counterfactual_proposals.py}.

The manuscript separates four evidence classes:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item exploratory design evidence, used to motivate components but never
  pooled into the final method comparison;
  \item the incomplete registered ModeBench campaign, reported only at paired
  shared preregistered checkpoints;
  \item the terminal six-run MathIR causal ablation; and
  \item invalidated or failed successor cohorts, retained in the repository
  but excluded from every headline estimate.
\end{enumerate}

\end{document}
